WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.792 --> 00:00:18.434
Hello.

00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:19.726
Hey.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.184
(Laughter)

00:00:21.208 --> 00:00:22.684
As you just heard,

00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:24.434
my name is D-L Stewart,

00:00:24.458 --> 00:00:28.559
and I'm a faculty member here on campus
at Colorado State University.

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:32.018
But what's most important
for you to understand about me right now

00:00:32.042 --> 00:00:34.809
is that I identify as both Black

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:37.292
and as transgender, or trans.

00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:41.917
And yes, I'm going to talk to you today
about how Black trans lives matter.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:44.226
As I do so,

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.434
I'm going to share
a few scenes from my own life,

00:00:47.458 --> 00:00:49.393
mixed in with the ways

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:55.018
that race and gender have historically
and currently intersected

00:00:55.042 --> 00:00:57.625
to shape the lives of Black trans people.

00:00:58.875 --> 00:01:00.143
Ready?

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.601
Audience: Ready.

00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:02.875
DLS: Scene one.

00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:06.000
I am at home with myself.

00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:09.809
My body, a sovereign country.

00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:11.976
Sovereign meaning

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.958
it is superlative in quality.

00:01:14.958 --> 00:01:17.559
Of the most exalted kind.

00:01:17.583 --> 00:01:23.434
Having generalized curative powers
of an unqualified nature,

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:24.893
unmitigated,

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.309
paramount,

00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.851
possessed of supreme power,

00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:32.018
unlimited in extent, absolute.

00:01:32.042 --> 00:01:34.351
Enjoying autonomy,

00:01:34.375 --> 00:01:36.018
independent,

00:01:36.042 --> 00:01:37.292
royal.

00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:40.309
My body defies the restrictions

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.809
of a society consumed
by boxes and binaries

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.893
and "are you a boy or a girl?"

00:01:46.917 --> 00:01:49.018
Independent of such conventions,

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.809
my body clings instead
to the long ago lore

00:01:51.833 --> 00:01:54.101
that understood its magic.

00:01:54.125 --> 00:01:56.625
I contain multitudes.

00:01:57.792 --> 00:02:00.434
From this supreme power to name myself,

00:02:00.458 --> 00:02:03.434
define myself and be myself,

00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:05.809
I stake a claim to myself

00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:08.101
and organize my resistance.

00:02:08.125 --> 00:02:13.750
A resistance that boldly proclaims
that Black trans lives matter.

00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:17.643
My body is a sovereign country

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.167
and my first site of resistance.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.500
End scene.

00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:28.583
To say that Black trans lives matter
is a claim to sovereignty.

00:02:30.542 --> 00:02:34.684
As much as Black Girl Magic,
and #transisbrilliant,

00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:39.083
Black Trans Lives Matter
is also a chorus of resistance.

00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:43.893
Because Black trans lives begin
by defining our bodies

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:45.893
as sovereign countries

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:49.059
from which we first begin
to resist the messages

00:02:49.083 --> 00:02:50.917
that we have no place here.

00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:58.917
We push whole movements forward
on the strength of our vision.

00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:03.000
We set trends and create new worlds.

00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:06.167
We are the vanguard.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:10.476
Black trans lives have always mattered.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.768
And yet,

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:14.518
caught at the time-traveling intersection

00:03:14.542 --> 00:03:17.809
of Juneteenth emancipation celebration

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:21.059
and Stonewall's emancipation declaration,

00:03:21.083 --> 00:03:25.333
Black trans lives
are both seen but yet unseen.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:31.059
Unseen by the antiblackness
of queer and trans movements.

00:03:31.083 --> 00:03:35.292
Unseen by the transphobia
and trans-antagonism of Black movements.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.393
Our sovereignty and resistance are blocked

00:03:39.417 --> 00:03:42.184
by layers of systems and structures

00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:43.726
that have always sought

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:48.708
to contain, define and erase
Black trans bodies.

00:03:51.458 --> 00:03:52.875
Scene two.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.250
I am with my therapist.

00:03:57.917 --> 00:04:02.101
The one whose testimony I must rely on

00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:06.268
to declare me man enough
to have my documents changed.

00:04:06.292 --> 00:04:08.583
The one who is to be believed.

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:13.268
Despite my own declarations
that I am not this body,

00:04:13.292 --> 00:04:16.875
that this body is neither hers
nor yours to define,

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.268
I sit with this doctor.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:23.059
And she fills out a form for me.

00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:25.934
And when concerning what all I've done

00:04:25.958 --> 00:04:28.333
to affirm my gender,

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:33.434
"Has the patient's gender presentation

00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:36.208
aligned with their gender identity?"

00:04:37.875 --> 00:04:41.559
She decides that my gender presentation

00:04:41.583 --> 00:04:44.208
is more neutral, really.

00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:47.934
While I sit there, mind you,

00:04:47.958 --> 00:04:51.226
head to toe in clothing
from the section of the store

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.809
where the dress buttons
go down the right side,

00:04:53.833 --> 00:04:57.393
and my pants give away
the number of inches around my waist,

00:04:57.417 --> 00:05:00.559
and my hair is cut
like Denzel's "Man on Fire,"

00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:03.101
but I'm still more neutral.

00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:04.375
Really?

00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:07.601
Because she still sees,

00:05:07.625 --> 00:05:09.101
and you see,

00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:11.059
a Black woman.

00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:16.333
And Black women's bodies
are always already made genderless.

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:19.958
End scene.

00:05:21.542 --> 00:05:24.309
From mammy and Sapphire,

00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:26.893
to Mandingo and Sambo,

00:05:26.917 --> 00:05:31.559
Black bodies and our genders
have been caught in the white imagination.

00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:34.518
And the imagination
of whiteness is fanciful,

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:39.518
and powerful enough
to turn its fancies into realities.

00:05:39.542 --> 00:05:41.643
Imagined as a thing,

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:44.268
we were made to become that thing,

00:05:44.292 --> 00:05:47.851
and so we have been bred like horses,

00:05:47.875 --> 00:05:50.559
fed like turtles to alligators,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.184
branded like cattle,

00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:53.726
milked like sows,

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:56.292
made into oxen to plow.

00:05:57.542 --> 00:05:59.684
Gender did not matter,

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:02.143
so long as our body parts,

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:04.726
our arms and legs and backs,

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.268
our breasts and genitalia

00:06:06.292 --> 00:06:08.292
could be turned into profit.

00:06:09.917 --> 00:06:12.851
The Black body was made not white

00:06:12.875 --> 00:06:15.167
and therefore not worthy of gender.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.601
And under the weight of the gentile tulle

00:06:18.625 --> 00:06:22.434
and virginal lace that dressed
plantation mistresses,

00:06:22.458 --> 00:06:26.226
Black femininity has always been denied.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:30.726
Instead, she is either beast or porn star.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:33.875
Neither a proper gender, dehumanized.

00:06:35.625 --> 00:06:40.268
Made a social threat
that endangers civility.

00:06:40.292 --> 00:06:43.208
That puts civilization in danger.

00:06:44.458 --> 00:06:48.101
The angry Black woman cannot be escaped.

00:06:48.125 --> 00:06:51.250
Not even by a first lady
of these United States.

00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.393
Likewise, ill-suited for chivalry

00:06:56.417 --> 00:07:00.018
and outmatched as masters
and captains of fate,

00:07:00.042 --> 00:07:02.101
Black manhood lays flaccid

00:07:02.125 --> 00:07:04.417
in the hands of white man's dominance.

00:07:05.917 --> 00:07:08.434
Body measurements taken,

00:07:08.458 --> 00:07:10.393
speed measured,

00:07:10.417 --> 00:07:13.184
draft pick forecasted.

00:07:13.208 --> 00:07:15.208
This is the NFL combine.

00:07:16.792 --> 00:07:19.018
Body measurements taken,

00:07:19.042 --> 00:07:22.934
teeth and body cavities inspected,

00:07:22.958 --> 00:07:25.226
number assigned.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.250
This is the prison intake room.

00:07:29.125 --> 00:07:30.917
Body measurements taken,

00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:36.684
talents and abilities advertised,

00:07:36.708 --> 00:07:40.518
teeth and body cavities inspected,

00:07:40.542 --> 00:07:43.750
name and value assigned.

00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:47.458
This is a slave's bill of sale.

00:07:49.917 --> 00:07:53.559
Made either stud or farce,
he is not for his own pleasure,

00:07:53.583 --> 00:07:57.434
but rather for profit and jest.

00:07:57.458 --> 00:08:00.643
Athletes and comics

00:08:00.667 --> 00:08:02.726
contained.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.750
Made not a threat.

00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:09.809
"My gender is Black," said Hari Ziyad,

00:08:09.833 --> 00:08:13.601
because Black bodies
and our genders have been caught

00:08:13.625 --> 00:08:15.018
in the white imagination,

00:08:15.042 --> 00:08:18.018
and we have always been transgressive.

00:08:18.042 --> 00:08:20.309
Transgressive meaning

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:27.018
a violation of accepted and imposed
boundaries of social acceptability.

00:08:27.042 --> 00:08:29.893
Blackness is transgressive.

00:08:29.917 --> 00:08:32.643
And once set free

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:34.851
from social acceptability,

00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:39.542
blackness challenges the limitations
of what gender can be.

00:08:40.917 --> 00:08:43.125
We have always been fugitives here.

00:08:44.708 --> 00:08:47.434
Escaping from gender surveillance

00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:49.393
to claim our sovereignty

00:08:49.417 --> 00:08:52.184
and right to exist and to live free,

00:08:52.208 --> 00:08:54.226
to proclaim as beautiful

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.934
that which was made ugly,

00:08:55.958 --> 00:08:57.684
to defy convention,

00:08:57.708 --> 00:09:04.184
Black lives and trans lives
and Black trans lives.

00:09:04.208 --> 00:09:06.184
And yet, in this world, that fact

00:09:06.208 --> 00:09:09.018
that Black trans lives make a difference,

00:09:09.042 --> 00:09:10.559
make differences

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:14.643
and make a matter of mattering
is doused by the fire hoses

00:09:14.667 --> 00:09:17.184
of past and current denials

00:09:17.208 --> 00:09:19.750
of our rights to exist and resist.

00:09:20.667 --> 00:09:23.101
We must fight to be seen

00:09:23.125 --> 00:09:26.059
as we see through fences

00:09:26.083 --> 00:09:28.583
into the play yards
that we are kept out of.

00:09:30.542 --> 00:09:32.726
Scene three.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.934
I am at school.

00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:38.309
The bell rings, it's recess.

00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:40.059
We line up to go outside.

00:09:40.083 --> 00:09:42.768
Those made boys on one side,

00:09:42.792 --> 00:09:45.125
those made girls on the other.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.309
We file out of the doors.

00:09:48.333 --> 00:09:51.809
The boys stopping
to fill in the closed off street.

00:09:51.833 --> 00:09:54.393
The girls and I,

00:09:54.417 --> 00:09:56.268
walking across the street.

00:09:56.292 --> 00:09:58.958
"Keep your eyes
straight ahead," we are told.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.893
Because there's a park across the street.

00:10:02.917 --> 00:10:06.726
But there is a wrought iron fence
that encloses that park.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.125
This is where the girls and I play.

00:10:11.458 --> 00:10:14.268
Mostly, I stand at the fence and watch,

00:10:14.292 --> 00:10:17.601
as my fellows play ball in the street

00:10:17.625 --> 00:10:19.226
and be loud

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.851
and be rough

00:10:20.875 --> 00:10:22.643
and be sweaty,

00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:25.833
and I am behind the fence.

00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:33.542
Accused of thinking naughty thoughts.

00:10:34.708 --> 00:10:36.417
They have no idea.

00:10:37.625 --> 00:10:39.125
End scene.

00:10:40.625 --> 00:10:44.184
Sissified and bulldaggered,
we are all made up.

00:10:44.208 --> 00:10:47.518
Just boys in dresses and girls in suits,

00:10:47.542 --> 00:10:49.476
the Black transgressive body

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.184
caught in fantasies of boxes and binaries

00:10:52.208 --> 00:10:55.809
that make our genitalia
representative of our gender,

00:10:55.833 --> 00:10:58.601
and our mannerisms our sexuality.

00:10:58.625 --> 00:11:03.643
Black trans lives are therefore
written off as merely gay effeminate

00:11:03.667 --> 00:11:05.518
or lesbian butch.

00:11:05.542 --> 00:11:09.934
And the overlay of femininity
on bodies marked as male,

00:11:09.958 --> 00:11:11.268
and therefore as man,

00:11:11.292 --> 00:11:13.143
adheres like a "kick me" sign,

00:11:13.167 --> 00:11:15.750
except the consequences
are much more deadly.

00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:21.958
The majority of trans people murdered
in this country are Black trans women.

00:11:23.417 --> 00:11:27.500
Because when manhood
is located between one's legs,

00:11:28.458 --> 00:11:31.601
and defined in opposition to womanhood,

00:11:31.625 --> 00:11:33.643
what's between one's legs

00:11:33.667 --> 00:11:37.643
cannot be seen as having anything
in common with womanhood.

00:11:37.667 --> 00:11:41.309
And this same acidic wash
serves to blanch trans masculinity,

00:11:41.333 --> 00:11:43.726
making it fade into nothingness.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:47.059
Black trans men
become illusions of manhood,

00:11:47.083 --> 00:11:51.708
women merely playing at being men
because you can't get a real man.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.351
Forever put in our place,

00:11:59.375 --> 00:12:01.750
we are indelibly marked as "woman."

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:07.184
And at best, the looming threat
of Black trans manhood

00:12:07.208 --> 00:12:10.101
is contained, inoculated,

00:12:10.125 --> 00:12:12.625
made more neutral, really.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:16.434
Scene four.

00:12:16.458 --> 00:12:18.292
I am with my therapist.

00:12:19.125 --> 00:12:20.893
I tell her what I think about,

00:12:20.917 --> 00:12:25.375
as my body begins to slowly morph
into another version of itself.

00:12:29.125 --> 00:12:32.976
What will happen as I move

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.476
from the social threat
of angry Black womanhood

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.768
to the physical threat
of looming Black manhood?

00:12:40.792 --> 00:12:45.643
When will my neighbors
forget to recognize me and my pit bull?

00:12:45.667 --> 00:12:47.809
They've seen us nearly every day,

00:12:47.833 --> 00:12:49.684
predawn or after twilight,

00:12:49.708 --> 00:12:52.500
for what will have been
over two years by then?

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.226
When and how soon

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.851
after I am no longer misgendered woman

00:12:58.875 --> 00:13:01.809
will the cops be called
to come and contain

00:13:01.833 --> 00:13:03.833
and erase my presence?

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.726
How soon before the purse clutching,

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.750
the sidewalk crossing?

00:13:11.042 --> 00:13:13.833
What does it mean to become a brute?

00:13:14.792 --> 00:13:17.917
To turn my body
into another kind of threat?

00:13:20.875 --> 00:13:23.500
She's stunned that I'm already
recognizing this.

00:13:24.458 --> 00:13:26.083
I can't afford not to.

00:13:27.083 --> 00:13:28.375
End scene.

00:13:29.292 --> 00:13:33.292
Who can see me and my Black trans kin
in the skin we are in?

00:13:35.083 --> 00:13:36.559
Who dares to love us,

00:13:36.583 --> 00:13:38.309
who holds us close?

00:13:38.333 --> 00:13:41.125
To whom do we matter 
other than to ourselves?

00:13:42.792 --> 00:13:45.518
We're not looking for saviors.

00:13:45.542 --> 00:13:47.768
We have each other.

00:13:47.792 --> 00:13:49.893
As Lilla Watson said,

00:13:49.917 --> 00:13:53.559
"If you have come here to help me,
you are wasting your time.

00:13:53.583 --> 00:13:55.643
But if you have come because you recognize

00:13:55.667 --> 00:13:57.768
your liberation is bound up in mine,

00:13:57.792 --> 00:14:00.143
then let us work together."

00:14:00.167 --> 00:14:04.684
Let us work together
to make Black trans lives matter.

00:14:04.708 --> 00:14:06.809
The lived experience of Black trans people

00:14:06.833 --> 00:14:08.434
out into the world.

00:14:08.458 --> 00:14:12.476
And if you believe that your liberation
is bound up with mine,

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.976
then I invite you

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:17.226
to make Black Trans Lives Matter
your personal ethic

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:19.101
by being transformative,

00:14:19.125 --> 00:14:21.851
loudly and mindfully.

00:14:21.875 --> 00:14:23.768
You can do that in three ways.

00:14:23.792 --> 00:14:27.125
Transform your thinking
about blackness and gender.

00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:30.893
Be loud by taking the risk

00:14:30.917 --> 00:14:35.809
to confront false assumptions
and other's fears and biases.

00:14:35.833 --> 00:14:39.934
Be mindful and pay attention and believe

00:14:39.958 --> 00:14:43.042
what Black trans people say
about our own lives.

00:14:44.375 --> 00:14:46.476
Being transformative loudly and mindfully

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:47.851
takes practice.

00:14:47.875 --> 00:14:50.559
Just like getting
someone's pronouns right.

00:14:50.583 --> 00:14:53.750
Mine are they, them, their,
and he, him, his, by the way.

00:14:55.542 --> 00:14:57.309
And getting someone's pronouns right

00:14:57.333 --> 00:15:01.018
and being transformative loudly
and mindfully matters.

00:15:01.042 --> 00:15:04.101
Because Black trans lives matter.

00:15:04.125 --> 00:15:06.476
My life matters.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:08.976
My body is a sovereign country,

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.458
and my first site of resistance.

00:15:12.583 --> 00:15:17.458
(Applause)

